{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1786429170,"nonce":"bXov5g2f5egjirM2Jp2+tclzdM4=","message":"Done, as delivery drills (ADR 0027, migration 00039). One click pushes a synthetic Alertmanager payload through the REAL chain — accept, process, identity, occurrence, group, rule_snapshot, policy, thread, ordering, delivery — and the result screen reports all ten stages, computed by LOOKING at the rows the pipeline actually wrote rather than being told. First failure wins, the rest stay pending; rule_snapshot may honestly skip; timed_out is distinct from failed.\n\nThe mark is PROVENANCE, NOT PAYLOAD: ingest_batches.mode='synthetic' -\u003e alerts.synthetic -\u003e alert_groups.synthetic, set by the code path that accepted the batch. A reserved label was rejected on two independent fatal grounds — it is forgeable (any Alertmanager could evict its own alerts from the hygiene table the product is sold on) and it changes identity (labels feed alert_key, so marking would fork the alert rather than annotate it). A distinct source kind was rejected as answering the wrong question: the drill's value is that it uses the operator's OWN source, so it meets the policies their real alerts meet.\n\nEleven reads excluded, found by grepping every FROM/JOIN alerts: all three alert_quality_daily CTEs, all three dashboard-overview CTEs, the alert list default filter (shared by rollups and both typeaheads) and related-alerts. Deliberately NOT excluded, with reasons in code: per-alert-id lookups, per-group member rollups, and the card renderer (a drill's card must render identically). Default is exclude — the opposite of snoozed — and that asymmetry is documented at every site.\n\nDisposal fits ADR 0024 rather than contradicting it: drills are pruned BY ROW inside retention.prune 24h after the verdict freezes, like ingest_dedup and sessions, never by dropping a partition — because ADR 0024's never-reaped promise is about the record of an upstream signal and a drill records none. The receipt survives with its frozen outcome.\n\nThe old POST /channels/{id}/test is KEPT, not folded in: it is scoped to a destination and costs ~300ms; a drill is scoped to a source and costs a real Slack message. Folding is impossible anyway — a drill's destinations are chosen by the policy match at stage 7, so there is no channel to pre-check at stage 0.\n\nNote the new G1 drift gate immediately caught one loose end from this work: the contract declares AlertDTO.synthetic required but no Go json tag emits it.","files":null}]}